 {
  "content": [
   {
    "text": "I labelled 1 column for job 1, but the file is mis-parsed and the label doesn't describe the real data.\n\nThe file is semicolon-delimited, but the contract reads it as comma-delimited. So the whole header lands in one column. That column holds nine fields: member_id, first_name, last_name, dob, sex, plan_code, coverage_start, coverage_end and patient_ref. The profile stores it as `column_1`, so I reported it under that name, with `phi: true` and role `other`.\n\nBecause the fields are merged, the file's real columns can't be labelled yet. The vendor or the contract needs to fix the delimiter first. Once it's split, the individual columns should be profiled again. Several of them are PHI: names, dob, member_id and patient_ref.",
    "type": "text"
   }
  ],
